androidagent 0.4.0

This is a modified version of Buddy by ghorbelhamdi and contributors.
Upstream: https://github.com/ghorbelhamdi/buddy-android
Base commit: 8c69699b1338f3b3c177979bbd0a69140bbdb9ce (Buddy 1.0.0)
Upstream and the application integration modifications are distributed under
Apache License 2.0. Separately bundled runtime components retain their licenses.

Modifications (2026-10-09): separate application identity and MCP port;
conversation-first androidagent UI; Codex defaults; device metrics; bounded local
shell with per-command approvals; rich message rendering; draft preservation;
ARM64/x86_64 Codex launcher; device instrumentation tests and build scripts.
Additional modifications (2026-10-10): Claude Code ARM64/x86_64 musl runtime
setup, backend selection, streamed responses, isolated sessions, CLI auth status,
model aliases, Remote Control MCP policy and integration coverage. Runtime downloads
are separate: official Anthropic npm packages and Alpine musl (MIT), not bundled.
Java package paths were moved from app.buddy.assistant to dev.mateuszsury.androidagent.

Geist and Geist Mono fonts: SIL Open Font License, bundled in
app/src/main/assets/fonts/OFL-Geist.txt.
Material Symbols icons: Apache License 2.0 (upstream).

androidagent is an independent community application. It is not an official
OpenAI or Anthropic application. Codex, ChatGPT and Claude belong to their
respective owners. No provider credentials or model binaries are bundled.

Additional modifications (2026-10-10): own local Linux VM lifecycle, Docker
task controller, native project UI, shared Codex/Claude MCP tools, artifact
export and task cleanup. QEMU/SeaBIOS, Linux and Alpine packages are separately
licensed runtime components; see docker/SOURCES.md and docker/licenses.

Additional modifications (2026-10-10): shared MCP host independent of
Accessibility, per-run USB grants, native UART and ESP flashing, USB ADB,
SAF storage, scoped USB redirection into Docker and a task-bound UART bridge.
usb-serial-for-android by mik3y and contributors retains its MIT license.
esp-serial-flasher by Espressif and contributors retains its Apache-2.0 license.
Pinned sources, adaptations and notices: usb/README.md, usb/sources.json,
usb/licenses and the original copyright notices in vendored source files.
libusb and usbredir retain their separately documented runtime licenses
under docker/licenses and docker/SOURCES.md.
